Other remarks:

	Amulets / helms of ESP do nothing, even if the player is
polymorphed.  They work for all other races, even if the other
race is polyed into an automaton.

	Remember to add an automaton monster.  Acid potions should
do major damage.

	Damage does not heal normally.  Have a repair kit?  (A repair
kit with charges might make the game nearly unplayable.  A repair kit
with unlimited charges changes healing from "happens automatically"
to "a boring manual process".)  Or a tool kit, and the ability to 
make replacement parts out of metal objects?  (This is a lot more
promising.  "3 hit points left!  I need 40 pounds of iron, or it's
game over!"  Using a ring as a source of metal is the same as eating
the ring.)

	Demons are peaceful towards you:  you don't have a soul,
so why bother?  However, they won't wind you up, either:  you don't
have a soul to trade away, so why bother?  (Exception:  the quest
nemesis is always hostile.)

	Automatons cannot make dogs or cats into pets by throwing
food.  Animals don't form an emotional bond with a walking lump of
metal that easily.

	If your mainspring winds all the way down AND you have an
intelligent pet with hands on the level, the game doesn't end until
the pet dies OR some hostile monster smashes you into scrap metal.
If your pet gets adjacent to you before this, he winds you up and
the game continues.


